      "intent": {
        "task": "Judge integer existence using divisibility, integrality, factorization and nonzero domains.",
        "source_solution": "The first fails divisibility by 3 and the third fails integrality of xy. The second has (1,13); the fourth has exactly (8,1),(8,-1); the fifth has (12,12), more generally x=6+d,y=6+36/d for integer divisors d of 36 except -6; the sixth has x=+-6,y=+-5 independently.",
        "unit_reason": "The original is one shared integer-existence classification; all six equations remain together.",
